      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two patients with functional single ventricle and a left superior vena cava, which drained to the coronary sinus, are presented. Each had undergone a Fontan modification that incorporated the coronary sinus into the Fontan pathway. Each developed severe right atrial and coronary sinus dilatation. Revision of a Fontan with an intraatrial lateral tunnel and an extracardiac conduit resulted in improved functional capacity of the patients."},
